.whyline/relay/chat-history.jsonl:11:{"agent": "grok", "prompt": "Research \"Now I want you to analyse the current capability of sonde and I want to add feature like https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify offers using which it becomes more useful something like I cna create a .md file plus ismilar to archfy on demand, reason so that sonde can be useful for the AI agents, developers and vibe coders who do not have understanding of the code so we have to make thme a way they can understand how there project or prgam works so that they can better undersatnd whats going inside . So lets do  brainstorm and create a plan for modifying sonde and making it much more useful\" independently. Write your findings to /Users/anish/CodeGraph/.whyline/relay/brainstorm-tmp/grok.md as plain markdown. This is your own independent pass -- you haven't seen, and shouldn't need, any other model's perspective yet.", "response": "I'll research Sonde's current capabilities and Archify independently, then write a plan to `grok.md`. Starting with the project, Archify, and the brainstorming skill.This is architectural research: I'll map Sonde's current surface, study Archify, then write an independent plan to `grok.md` without looking at the other model files.Sonde already has `doc` and `map`; next I\u2019ll compare those against Archify\u2019s skill, IR, and viewer so the plan targets the actual gap.I have enough to write an independent capability analysis and phased plan. Drafting `grok.md` next.Independent research is in [`.whyline/relay/brainstorm-tmp/grok.md`](/Users/anish/CodeGraph/.whyline/relay/brainstorm-tmp/grok.md).\n\nThe main finding: Sonde already has the Markdown and interactive HTML this request describes (`sonde doc` \u2192 `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `sonde map` \u2192 `ARCHITECTURE.html`). The gap is the Archify loop \u2014 on-demand, scoped, skill-invoked, readable without already knowing the architecture.\n\nThe plan is: stop hiding `doc`/`map`, put a skill in front of them, give MCP the