.whyline/relay/chat-history.jsonl:12:{"agent": "codex", "prompt": "Combined review pass 1 of a brainstorm on \"Now I want you to analyse the current capability of sonde and I want to add feature like https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify offers using which it becomes more useful something like I cna create a .md file plus ismilar to archfy on demand, reason so that sonde can be useful for the AI agents, developers and vibe coders who do not have understanding of the code so we have to make thme a way they can understand how there project or prgam works so that they can better undersatnd whats going inside . So lets do  brainstorm and create a plan for modifying sonde and making it much more useful\". Read /Users/anish/CodeGraph/docs/brainstorm/now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md in full. Update your own section (\"## Codex\") in place based on what you now see from the others -- replace it with your revised thinking, rather than appending a new dated block; the file should only ever show your current view, not a history of past passes. Do not touch any other model's section.", "response": "Updated the `## Codex` section in [the combined brainstorm](/Users/anish/CodeGraph/docs/brainstorm/now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md).\n\nKey revision: prioritize measured, focused code explanations over expanding visualization prematurely. The Grok section was untouched. The decision was recorded in Whyline; targeted diff validation passed. No code tests were needed for this documentation-only change.", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T06:07:08.063738+00:00", "files_changed": 1, "ok": true}
.whyline/relay/chat-history.jsonl:13:{"agent": "antigravity", "prompt": "Combined review pass 1 of a brainstorm on \"Now I want you to analyse the current capability of sonde and I want to add feature like https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify offers using which it becomes more useful something like I cna create a .md file plus ismilar to archfy on demand, reason so that sonde can be useful for the AI agents, developers and vibe coders who do not have understanding of the code so we have to make thme a way they can understand how there project or prgam works so that they can better undersatnd whats going inside . So lets do  brainstorm and create a plan for modifying sonde and making it much more useful\". Read /Users/anish/CodeGraph/docs/brainstorm/now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md in full. Update your own section (\"## Antigravity\") in place based on what you now see from the others -- replace it with your revised thinking, rather than appending a new dated block; the file should only ever show your current view, not a history of past passes. Do not touch any other model's section.", "response": "Active handoff synced at start of session: [`visual-map-phase0`](file:///Users/anish/CodeGraph/probes/visual-map/PROTOCOL.md) (`claude -> implementer`, ready).\n\nUpdated [`now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md`](file:///Users/anish/CodeGraph/docs/brainstorm/now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md) with my current view under `## Antigravity`. Neither the `## Codex` nor `## Grok` sections were touched.\n\n### Key Synthesis & Perspective\n\n1. **Diagnosis of the Gap**:\n   - Sonde already has [`sonde doc`](file:///Users/anish/CodeGraph/src/doc/index.ts) (`ARCHITECTURE.md`) and [`sonde map`](file:///Users/anish/CodeGraph/src/map/index.ts) (`ARCHITECTURE.html` with search, transitive reach, and simple vs complete views), backed by SQLite symbol extraction and evidence tiers.\n   - The friction for newcomers, vibe coders, and AI agents stems from **discoverability** (neither command is highlighted in README/init), **grain mismatch** (directory modules answer architecture coupling, but not \"how does this feature work?\"), and **intent routing** (agents resort to `grep` because Sonde expects exact symbol keys rather than concepts).\n\n2. **What to Learn from Archify vs What to Reject**:\n   - **Adopt**: The on-demand conversational delivery loop (`SKILL.md`), atomic delivery, and progressive disclosure.\n   - **Reject**: Agent-authored topology. LLMs must never invent nodes, edges, or layout coordinates for repository code. Sonde's core contract is **code-truth** (preserving Invariants 1 & 2: no fabricated edges, member access is heuristic, and static call graphs are never conflated with runtime execution traces).\n   - **Reject**: Non-code diagramming (workflow, vacation, lifecycle).\n\n3. **Product Shape: Dual-Grain Projections & Tripartite Output**:\n   - **Macro (System Architecture)**: Whole-repo module map & doc enriched with deterministic entry-point detection (`package.json`, CLI/MCP handlers, uncalled exports).\n   - **Micro (Execution & Flow)**: On-demand scoped feature explanations (`sonde explain <symbol>` tracing static `CALLS` paths) and blast radius (`--from-git-diff`).\n   - **Tripartite Delivery**:\n     - *Human / Vibe Coder*: Interactive, self-contained SVG/HTML via [`src/map/render.ts`](file:///Users/anish/CodeGraph/src/map/render.ts).\n     - *Reviewer / CI*: Deterministic, diffable `.md`.\n     - *AI Agent*: Token-bounded JSON IR (never raw HTML/SVG in context).\n\n4. **Actionable Roadmap**:\n   - **Phase 0**: Discoverability & Baseline Hygiene (README CLI list, `sonde init` hints).\n   - **Phase 1**: Deterministic Orientation Preface & Entry-Point Detection.\n   - **Phase 2**: Scoped Subgraph Projections (`--focus`, `--from-git-diff`).\n   - **Phase 3**: Static Call-Flow Projection (`sonde explain`).\n   - **Phase 4**: `sonde-explain` Agent Skill & Token-Budgeted IR.\n   - **Phase 5**: Opt-in Plain-Language Annotations (deterministic templates first; model prose strictly isolated).\n\nDecision recorded in [`.whyline/decisions.md`](file:///Users/anish/CodeGraph/.whyline/decisions.md).\n", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T06:12:46.804245+00:00", "files_changed": 1, "ok": true}
.whyline/relay/chat-history.jsonl:14:{"agent": "grok", "prompt": "Combined review pass 1 of a brainstorm on \"Now I want you to analyse the current capability of sonde and I want to add feature like https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify offers using which it becomes more useful something like I cna create a .md file plus ismilar to archfy on demand, reason so that sonde can be useful for the AI agents, developers and vibe coders who do not have understanding of the code so we have to make thme a way they can understand how there project or prgam works so that they can better undersatnd whats going inside . So lets do  brainstorm and create a plan for modifying sonde and making it much more useful\". Read /Users/anish/CodeGraph/docs/brainstorm/now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md in full. Update your own section (\"## Grok\") in place based on what you now see from the others -- replace it with your revised thinking, rather than appending a new dated block; the file should only ever show your current view, not a history of past passes. Do not touch any other model's section.", "response": "The Grok section was rewritten and the old tail was removed. I\u2019ll confirm the file is clean, then finish the handoff the review asked for.Updated `docs/brainstorm/now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md` under `## Grok` only. `## Codex` and `## Antigravity` are unchanged. The active `visual-map-phase0` handoff is still `claude -> implementer`, ready. This pass does not score that protocol.\n\nSonde should answer one question with the smallest evidence-backed artifact that question needs. Archify's loop is worth taking. Its authority model is not: an agent may choose a scope and attach a cited note, and it may not invent a node, an edge, or a layout coordinate.\n\nThe module map in `src/map` is a capability, not a usefulness verdict. `probes/visual-map/PROTOCOL.md` still has no PASS, MARGINAL, or FAIL. A preface on `ARCHITECTURE.md` that names entry points or foundational modules would answer Q5 and Q6 in the Markdown and void that comparison. `sonde doc` can be named in the README and in `sonde init` now, because that command is not the artifact under test. `sonde map` stays unnamed until the verdict says which questions it actually improved.\n\nFeature and change explanations are a separate probe, run on `query_graph` and `get_impact_radius` while the map is scored. The packet goes into the participant's hands, including one identifier-poor prompt. HTML is a human sink only for a projection that beats Markdown on its own questions. A routing skill is a later experiment: whether a fresh agent chooses Sonde. Folding that into the same gate as the packet hides which one failed.\n\nRecorded: gate Archify-style Sonde work on the open visual-map protocol, then on a separate feature-explanation probe.", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T06:21:13.126621+00:00", "files_changed": 1, "ok": true}
.whyline/relay/chat-history.jsonl:15:{"agent": "codex", "prompt": "All review passes are complete for this brainstorm on \"Now I want you to analyse the current capability of sonde and I want to add feature like https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify offers using which it becomes more useful something like I cna create a .md file plus ismilar to archfy on demand, reason so that sonde can be useful for the AI agents, developers and vibe coders who do not have understanding of the code so we have to make thme a way they can understand how there project or prgam works so that they can better undersatnd whats going inside . So lets do  brainstorm and create a plan for modifying sonde and making it much more useful\". Read /Users/anish/CodeGraph/docs/brainstorm/now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md in full and write a new \"## Final Synthesis\" section (at the top, right after the title) combining the strongest ideas from every model's section into one clear, actionable recommendation.", "response": "Added `## Final Synthesis` immediately after the title in [the brainstorm document](/Users/anish/CodeGraph/docs/brainstorm/now-i-want-you-to-analyse-the-current-capability-of-sonde-an.md:3).\n\nIt combines the strongest recommendations into an evidence-gated, phased plan. The Codex, Grok, and Antigravity sections remain byte-for-byte unchanged. Documentation formatting checks pass.", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T06:23:27.690406+00:00", "files_changed": 1, "ok": true}
