usage: whyline [-h] [--version] <command> ...

Records why your code exists, and tells the next agent.

positional arguments:
  <command>
    explain   Why does this code exist?
    note      Record a decision
    attach    Bind an earlier decision to the commit that implemented it
    retract   Withdraw a decision that turned out wrong (no replacement)
    decisions
              List, search or show recorded decisions
    ledger    Inspect, prune or change what the local ledger keeps
    doctor    Check everything whyline depends on here, with fixes
    handoff   Record an active-task handoff (or `handoff close` to close it)
    claim     Claim advisory task/file ownership
    release   Release advisory ownership
    brief     Summary for the next agent
    sync      Compact active-task handoff
    run       Launch an agent with active context attached
    relay     Run a plan through Codex and Claude unattended (needs the
              whyline-relay package).
    timeline  Project event history
    status    Is whyline healthy here?
    init      Set whyline up in this repository
    account   Detect which plan/tier codex and claude are authenticated under
    model     Choose which model each agent uses in this repo
    console   An editable multiline console for whyline and whyline-relay
    agents    Saved agents: list, run, history, schedule

options:
